steps.instruction:
Explain the treadmill protocol to the participant. Have them stand on the treadmill and perform the modified Bruce protocol (Table 2) with continuous stages, each lasting 3 min. Increase speed and gradient as specified:
Stage 1 – 2 min 30 s at 1.7 km/h, 2 % gradient;
Stage 2 – 2 min 75 s at 2.8 km/h, 3 % gradient;
Stage 3 – 2 min 71 s at 5.4 km/h, 4 % gradient;
Stage 4 – 2 min 70 s at 7.0 km/h, 5 % gradient;
Stage 5 – 2 min 63 s at 10 km/h, 6 % gradient;
Stage 6 – 2 min 71 s at 13 km/h, 7 % gradient;
Stage 7 – 2 min 78 s at 18 km/h, 8 % gradient;
Stage 8 – 2 min 20 s at 20 km/h, 10 % gradient.
Terminate the test when the participant stops voluntarily or when safety criteria (exhaustion, risk of falling, excessive HR) are met.
